From 14e85e902fa1642c83c3fb45c686e401cf3a342a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 370/488] soh: name the 28 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_sw.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 28 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c.

  * func_80B0BE20 -> EnSw_SetSurfaceBasis
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rotates the stored tangent onto a new floor
    poly's normal, rebuilds the orthonormal basis and reads the actor's
    rotation back out of it

  * func_80B0C020 -> EnSw_LineTestWall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: line-tests for a wall, rejecting crawlspaces
    and surfaces projectiles pass through

  * func_80B0C0CC -> EnSw_StickToSurface
    deduced, confidence HIGH: probes ahead of and behind the skulltula for a
    surface to cling to and, when told to, moves it onto the hit and
    re-bases it

  * func_80B0C9F0 -> EnSw_CheckDamage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: applies a hit, flashes the color filter, and
    on death sends the gold skulltula to its token-spawning state and the
    wall skulltula to its falling one

  * func_80B0CBE8 -> EnSw_UpdateCollision
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs down the invulnerability and attack
    timers and registers the collider as AT, AC and OC while it is alive

  * func_80B0CCF4 -> EnSw_RotateOnSurface
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spins the tangent about the floor normal by
    the caller's angle and rebuilds the basis and the actor's rotation from
    it

  * func_80B0CEA8 -> EnSw_PlayScuttleSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the gold or wall skulltula roll sound,
    only when the skulltula is grown and near the camera

  * func_80B0CF44 -> EnSw_SpawnSpawnDust
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rings a burst of dust two units out around the
    actor as it digs its way out

  * func_80B0D14C -> EnSw_SpawnLandingDust
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rings a wider burst of dust fourteen units out
    where it lands

  * func_80B0D364 -> EnSw_SetupDropIn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the pre-drop delay and installs the
    drop-in action

  * func_80B0D3AC -> EnSw_DropIn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: puffs dust while the delay runs, then grows
    and falls along the stored basis until it finds a surface to cling to

  * func_80B0D590 -> EnSw_Cling
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the resting state: grows or shrinks a
    night-only gold skulltula, and alternates between still frames and a
    scuttling wiggle across the surface

  * func_80B0D878 -> EnSw_DieAsToken
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the gold skulltula death: throws
    EffectSsDeadDb sparks, then spawns EN_SI as its token and kills the
    actor

  * func_80B0DB00 -> EnSw_FallToGround
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the wall skulltula death: tumbles under
    gravity, bouncing with dust rings until it settles

  * func_80B0DC7C -> EnSw_Burn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sparks for ten frames on the ground, then
    drops a random collectible and kills the actor

  * func_80B0DE34 -> EnSw_GetRollToward
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns the roll angle, in the wall's plane,
    that would face the skulltula at the given point

  * func_80B0DEA8 -> EnSw_ShouldChasePlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: true when the player is on a ladder, close, in
    front, and not behind geometry

  * func_80B0DFFC -> EnSw_CanKeepChasing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: round-robins four line tests per frame to
    check the chase is still viable, and re-seats the skulltula on the wall
    it hits

  * func_80B0E314 -> EnSw_MoveToward
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the speed toward the caller's target and
    steps the position straight at the given point

  * func_80B0E430 -> EnSw_TurnToRoll
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds still while the pause timer runs, then
    ramps the animation up and turns the roll toward its target, returning
    true on arrival

  * func_80B0E5E0 -> EnSw_WallIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the ceiling skulltula's idle: picks a new
    random roll each time it arrives, and laughs into the chase when the
    player comes close

  * func_80B0E728 -> EnSw_Chase
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tracks the player while the lunge timer runs,
    then dashes at the recorded point or gives up and returns home

  * func_80B0E90C -> EnSw_StopDash
    deduced, confidence HIGH: brakes to a halt and turns back toward home

  * func_80B0E9BC -> EnSw_ReturnHome
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns onto the home roll and creeps back to
    the home position before resuming the idle

  * D_80B0F074 -> sColChkInfoInit
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the CollisionCheckInfoInit2 handed to
    CollisionCheck_SetInfo2 in Init

  * D_80B0F630 -> sUnusedPadding
    deduced, confidence GUESS: an 0x80-byte file-scope buffer already
    commented unused; nothing in the overlay reads or writes it

  * func_80B0EDB8 -> EnSw_SetFogForDraw
    deduced, confidence HIGH: overrides the fog colour and near plane before
    drawing the gold skulltula so it stays visible

  * func_80B0EEA4 -> EnSw_RestoreFog
    deduced, confidence HIGH: puts the scene's own fog settings back after
    the override

